> Describe a system-on-chip in two sentences.
A system-on-chip (SoC) is a microprocessor or system designed to be integrated into a single integrated circuit (IC), typically a microprocessor chip, which is used to perform all the functions of a computer or other computing system, including data processing, memory management, communication, and other related functions.

